# Only used when the whole project is deployed as a literal git clone
# directly into the web server's document root (e.g. Hostinger's hPanel
# "GIT" deploy tool with Root Directory set to public_html — it does a
# plain `git clone`, with no Laravel-aware handling of the public/
# subfolder). In that layout this file sits next to app/, config/,
# vendor/, composer.json, etc. at the doc root, so without this rewrite
# every one of those would be directly downloadable/executable over
# HTTP. This transparently routes every request into public/ (Laravel's
# real front controller and its own .htaccess take it from there) and,
# just as importantly, makes anything NOT under public/ 404 instead of
# being served as a raw file.
#
# Harmless everywhere else: a normal deployment that points the document
# root straight at public/ (the preferred setup — see
# HOSTINGER_DEPLOYMENT.md) never has this file in its web root at all,
# and local dev (php artisan serve / Vite) never goes through Apache.
<IfModule mod_rewrite.c>
    RewriteEngine On
    RewriteCond %{REQUEST_URI} !^/public/
    RewriteRule ^(.*)$ public/$1 [L]
</IfModule>
